      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "AL'S MEMORY (7) was beaten for speed from wide out but attacked the line strongly to place, 4.5 lengths from the winner (30.03) at Richmond in Grade 5. Yet to miss the placings from three starts out of this box. Racing well and deserves a win. FASCINATE SUZIE (1) was in the placings last time but shapes well for this on her blistering win the start prior, getting around this track over 515m in 29.27. Top win two back and rates a key player again. WRECK IT REX (2) goes very well over this track and trip including two wins. Was out of the placings last time (35.22) at this track in a Grade 5, finishing fourth and beaten 12 lengths. Looks suited here and can measure up. WHY ME (8) is worth some thought after placing last start.",
